## Auth

### `POST /auth/register`
**Auth:** none
**Body:**
```json
{ "name": "Jane Doe", "email": "jane@example.com", "password": "at least 6 chars", "role": "student" }
```
`role` is optional — only `"student"` or `"instructor"` are accepted from the
public form; anything else (including `"admin"`) silently falls back to
`"student"`. This is intentional: admin accounts are never created through
open registration, see the README's "Create your first admin account" section.

**Response `201`:**
```json
{ "success": true, "message": "User registered successfully", "user": { "_id", "name", "email", "role" }, "token": "..." }
```

### `POST /auth/login`
**Auth:** none
**Body:** `{ "email": "jane@example.com", "password": "..." }`
**Response `200`:** same shape as register. `403` if the account has been deactivated.

